Update main.rs state machine to use MultiStreamPlayer instead of Player.

## Implementation

**File:** src/main.rs

### Changes to run_radio()
```rust
fn run_radio() -> Result<()> {
    // Replace Player with MultiStreamPlayer
    let mut player = audio::MultiStreamPlayer::new()?;

    // ... rest of setup ...

    loop {
        match state {
            RadioState::Welcome => {
                handle_welcome(&mut player, &tts);
            }
            RadioState::Playing(idx) => {
                let channel = &channels::CHANNELS[idx];
                // CHANGED: No play_stream(), just select()
                player.speak(channel.tts_name, &tts);
                player.select(idx);  // Instant switch
            }
            RadioState::Off => {
                // CHANGED: disconnect_all() to save bandwidth
                player.speak_sync("Radio off", &tts);
                player.disconnect_all();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Key differences from old Player
- `play_stream(url)` → `select(index)` - instant, no HTTP
- `stop()` → `disconnect_all()` - disconnects all streams to save bandwidth
- Streams reconnect in Welcome state via `connect_all()`

