Implement connect_all() method to connect all 4 streams at boot with timeout.

## Implementation

**File:** src/audio.rs

### Method signature
```rust
impl MultiStreamPlayer {
    /// Connect all streams at boot (blocking, with timeout)
    /// Returns number of successfully connected streams
    pub fn connect_all(&mut self, channels: &[Channel], timeout: Duration) -> usize;
}
```

### Behavior
1. Spawn 4 threads in parallel, one per channel
2. Each thread: HTTP connect + format probe + create decoder
3. Wait for all with timeout using channels (std::thread has no join_timeout)
4. Track status per stream (0=connecting, 1=playing, 2=error)
5. Return count of successfully connected streams

### Correct parallel connection pattern (using mpsc for timeout)
```rust
use std::sync::mpsc;
use std::time::Instant;

let (tx, rx) = mpsc::channel();

// Spawn threads that send result when done
for (i, ch) in channels.iter().enumerate() {
    let tx = tx.clone();
    let url = ch.url.to_string();
    thread::spawn(move || {
        let result = connect_single(i, &url);
        tx.send((i, result)).ok();
    });
}
drop(tx);  // Close sender so rx knows when all done

// Wait with timeout
let deadline = Instant::now() + timeout;
let mut connected = 0;
for _ in 0..channels.len() {
    let remaining = deadline.saturating_duration_since(Instant::now());
    match rx.recv_timeout(remaining) {
        Ok((i, Ok(stream))) => {
            self.streams[i] = Some(stream);
            connected += 1;
        }
        Ok((i, Err(e))) => {
            warn!("Failed to connect stream {}: {}", i, e);
        }
        Err(_) => break,  // Timeout
    }
}
connected
```

### Volume on connect
- All streams start muted (volume 0.0 / MUTED_VOLUME)
- Only active stream gets volume when select() called

Handle welcome on startup separately, then use simple loop: rx.recv() to block, drain extras, handle press. Eliminates confusing pending_press flag.

## Implementation

**File:** src/main.rs
**Location:** run_radio() function, lines 102-181

**Step 1:** Extract welcome logic to separate function:
```rust
fn handle_welcome(player: &mut audio::Player, tts: &std::sync::Arc<tts::PiperTts>) {
    info!("Welcome channel - checking for updates");
    player.speak_sync("Hello!", tts);
    player.speak_sync("Checking for updates. Please wait.", tts);
    // ... update check logic ...
    player.speak_sync("Press button to start radio.", tts);
}
```

**Step 2:** Simplify main loop:
```rust
// Handle welcome on startup (no button press needed)
handle_welcome(&mut player, &tts);

let mut channel_idx: usize = 0;  // 0 = first channel, after welcome

loop {
    // Wait for button press
    rx.recv().ok();
    while rx.try_recv().is_ok() {}  // Drain extras

    channel_idx += 1;
    let num_channels = channels::CHANNELS.len();

    if channel_idx > num_channels {
        // Off state
        player.stop();
        player.speak_sync("Radio off", &tts);
        channel_idx = 0;  // Reset, next press goes to welcome
        // Wait for next press to restart
        rx.recv().ok();
        while rx.try_recv().is_ok() {}
        handle_welcome(&mut player, &tts);
    } else {
        // Play channel
        let channel = &channels::CHANNELS[channel_idx - 1];
        player.speak(channel.tts_name, &tts);
        player.play_stream(channel.url)?;
    }
}
```

